From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:55:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 107/117] Revert "soundwire: qcom: force runtime suspend across
 system sleep"

Replaced by the signed version posted by Qualcomm (patchwork series 1215029
v2 for the LPASS LPI pinctrl part, series 1209436 for SoundWire), which do
the same thing (pm_runtime_force_suspend / _resume as system sleep ops);
ours was the armada-os form, carried without its author's Signed-off-by.

This reverts commit effd0a79a80b.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/soundwire/qcom.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
index a0189f6f3f48c..74bf23cd69e63 100644
--- a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
@@ -1926,7 +1926,6 @@ static int __maybe_unused swrm_runtime_suspend(struct device *dev)
 }
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops swrm_dev_pm_ops = {
-	SET_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend, pm_runtime_force_resume)
 	SET_RUNTIME_PM_OPS(swrm_runtime_suspend, swrm_runtime_resume, NULL)
 };
 
